From d747ee88c43457fdcdbdbdae9b70ec7f6200ef3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:40:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/amd/display: HDR over the tunnel as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12
 bits (DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TUNNEL_LAB)

The same property and meaning as i915 (linux-9933, drm_dvbridge_hdr10t.h),
for the tunnel of DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB on HDMI: the sink needs YCbCr 4:2:2
in its EDID, no Dolby block; HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA is required (the check of
the connector refuses it only without the property); the AVI InfoFrame says
YCbCr 4:2:2, BT.2020, limited range; the stream sends no Dolby VSIF in
vsp_infopacket, and its HDR static metadata packet goes out as for any HDR
stream; HDR10+ in its own packet where the mode has no HDMI VIC. It works on
every DCN, DCN 3.1 and 3.1.5 included (the tunnel needs no 4:2:2 from the
display core: the bytes are scanned out as RGB at 8 bits), which is what it is
for.

The checks of a tunnel are keyed on the Dolby VSIF in the stream
(amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_stream_active()): HDR over the tunnel has none, so a stream
that amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_fill_stream() made (byte_tunnel) counts as a tunnel,
and the scanout, output transfer function and dither checks apply to it as to
the others. A change of the property is a modeset. The reasons of a refusal go
to DVBRIDGE_REFUSED and the kernel log.

W=1 on amdgpu_dm, amdgpu_display: no warning. Not run on hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c   |   6 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_mode.h      |   2 +
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c |   5 +-
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.h |   7 +-
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 112 ++++++++++++++----
 .../amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_refused.c    |  23 +++-
 6 files changed, 127 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c
index 03549a199..9dc9310b7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c
@@ -1640,6 +1640,12 @@ int amdgpu_display_modeset_create_props(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 					 "DVBRIDGE_DV_HDMI14B_LAB");
 	if (!adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dv_hdmi14b_property)
 		return -ENOMEM;
+	/* Hades: HDR over that tunnel, as YCbCr 4:2:2 (drm_dvbridge_hdr10t.h) */
+	adev->mode_info.dvbridge_hdr10t_property =
+		drm_property_create_bool(adev_to_drm(adev), DRM_MODE_PROP_ATOMIC,
+					 "DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TUNNEL_LAB");
+	if (!adev->mode_info.dvbridge_hdr10t_property)
+		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	/* Hades: the same names and meanings as the i915 ones (drm_dvbridge_refused.h) */
 	adev->mode_info.dvbridge_hdr10_property =
